<title>USA: Saudi dissident indicted on conspiracy charges.</title>
<headline>Saudi dissident indicted on conspiracy charges.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Saudi dissident who agreed to cooperate with the FBI investigation into a deadly truck bombing in Saudi Arabia was charged on Wednesday with conspiracy to commit murder and &quot;international terrorism,&quot; the Justice Department said.</p>
<p>The indictment alleged that Hani Abdel-Rahim Hussein al-Sayegh, who was deported from Canada, &quot;was associated with a terrorist organization that actively promoted the use of violence&quot; against U.S. citizens and property abroad.</p>
</text>
